      "ts": "2026-02-14T12:49:44.697-08:00",
      "player": "Gem3P Villain",
      "type": "llm_response",
      "reasoning": "They cast `Lightning Strike` (presumably targeting me or my face, since my board is only lands and an enchantment).\n\
Target is not explicitly listed, but it's \"any target\". Typically face if I have no creatures.\n\
Should I counter `Lightning Strike`?\n\
It's 3 damage. I have 20 life.\n\
It's a burn spell.\n\
Is it worth `No More Lies`?\n\
`No More Lies` exiles the spell if paid (unless they pay 3). They have only 1 land untapped (`Rockface Village`). They cannot pay 3.\n\
Using a counterspell on a burn spell is generally card disadvantage unless the burn spell is lethal or killing a key permanent.\n\
My life is 20. Taking 3 down to 17 is fine.\n\
I should save `No More Lies` for a creature or a more impactful spell (like a planeswalker or a big draw spell, or something that generates board presence).\n\
They have 6 cards in hand. A simple 1-for-1 trade here is okay, but `No More Lies` is better used to stop them from developing a board I can't sweep easily, or protecting my future threats.\n\
Wait, if they are playing mono-red or similar red aggressive deck, burn spells ARE their win condition. But 3 damage for a card is a resource I can likely afford right now. I have `Day of Judgment` for creatures.\n\
I prefer to counter creatures that have haste or ETB effects, or planeswalkers.\n\
I will let `Lightning Strike` resolve.\n\
\n\
Action: Pass priority.\n\
\n\
