      "player": "Gem3P Villain",
      "type": "llm_response",
      "reasoning": "`Elspeth, Storm Slayer` is a 4 mana value planeswalker. Wait, my hand says `{3}{W}{W}` - that is 5 mana. The oracle check didn't return loyalty or cost because I asked by name and didn't check the object. Re-reading: \"mana_value:5\".\n\
Her text:\n\
+1: Create a 1/1 Soldier. (With passive, creates 2).\n\
It starts at? Probably 4 or 5 loyalty.\n\
If I tap out for Elspeth (5 mana), I have 0 left.\n\
Opponent has 3 mana open (2 Mountains, 1 Rockface). They have a lightning strike in grave. They might have another burn spell.\n\
If they just burn Elspeth, she dies or is low.\n\
If they play a creature with Haste (e.g. `Hired Claw` or `Monastery Swiftspear` equivalent), she dies.\n\
If I pass, I have `No More Lies` ({W}{U}) up.\n\
I can also activate `Fountainport` on their end step to make a Fish (3 mana). This is mana efficient. I can hold up NML, and if they do nothing worth countering, I make a Fish.\n\
This seems like the best line. Control 101: Draw-Go against aggro/midrange until you stabilise or they tap out.\n\
\n\
Action: Pass priority (decline to cast spells in my main phase).\n\
\n\
",
