    {
      "severity": "minor",
      "description": "Playing a Mountain instead of Rockface Village on turn 1 when casting a creature spell (Hired Claw). Rockface Village's creature-only red mana is sufficient for Hired Claw, and playing it first preserves unrestricted Mountains for later non-creature spells. Additionally, Rockface Village has a pump ability for Lizards like Hired Claw that becomes available sooner.",
      "action_taken": "Played a Mountain to cast Hired Claw",
      "better_line": "Play Rockface Village to cast Hired Claw (a creature), saving Mountains for later flexibility and getting the Lizard pump ability online earlier",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 7,
      "player": "MiniMx Libby",
      "decision_index": 5,
    },
    {
      "severity": "minor",
      "description": "Gem3P Villain has three lands in hand (Hallowed Fountain, Island, Plains) and only one land on the battlefield (Restless Anchorage). It's turn 2 and they need to make their land drop to curve toward Day of Judgment on turn 4 or No More Lies on turn 2. By not playing a land, they fall behind on mana development. Playing Hallowed Fountain (paying 2 life to have it enter untapped) would give them access to WU to hold up No More Lies this turn, which is particularly important since the opponent has a Mountain and could deploy threats.",
      "action_taken": "Skipped the land drop entirely, playing no land on turn 2.",
      "better_line": "Play Hallowed Fountain (paying 2 life for it to enter untapped) to hold up No More Lies as countermagic, or at minimum play any land untapped to not miss the land drop.",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 16,
      "player": "Gem3P Villain",
      "decision_index": 18,
    },
    {
      "severity": "minor",
      "description": "Playing Island instead of Plains with a hand containing Elspeth (3WW) and Day of Judgment (2WW) is slightly suboptimal. Playing Plains first maximizes white mana available on turn 4, which matters if they draw a 4th land and need to cast Day of Judgment (2WW), or if they need to activate Restless Anchorage (1WU) while also holding up No More Lies. Plains-first keeps more options open.",
      "action_taken": "Played Island as the third land drop.",
      "better_line": "Play Plains to have 3 white sources available sooner, better supporting the WW-heavy hand (Elspeth, Day of Judgment) and keeping Hallowed Fountain/Anchorage flexible for blue mana when needed.",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 24,
      "player": "Gem3P Villain",
      "decision_index": 25,
    },
    {
      "severity": "minor",
      "description": "Villain had an unplayed Island (or Fountainport) in hand. By playing a land first (making 6 lands), they could activate Restless Anchorage for {1}{W}{U} and still have 3 lands untapped - enough to hold up No More Lies ({W}{U}). Instead they passed, missing 2 damage and a Map token for free.",
      "action_taken": "Passed the turn without attacking or playing a land, reasoning that activating Restless Anchorage would prevent holding up No More Lies.",
      "better_line": "Play Island from hand, then activate Restless Anchorage to attack for 2 damage and create a Map token, while still having 3 untapped lands to hold up No More Lies.",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 32,
      "player": "Gem3P Villain",
      "decision_index": 37,
    },
    {
      "severity": "questionable",
      "description": "Declined to counter Lightning Strike with No More Lies when the opponent had only 1 land untapped (Rockface Village) and couldn't pay the {3} tax. The counter would have been guaranteed to exile the spell, saving 3 damage. While at 20 life 3 damage isn't critical, No More Lies is a cheap counterspell being used on a cheap spell - it's trading evenly on mana. However, saving the counter for a more impactful threat (like Nova Hellkite or Hexing Squelcher) is a reasonable argument, especially since Villain has Day of Judgment and Elspeth as powerful plays coming up. The decision is debatable but taking 3 unnecessary damage when you have a guaranteed counter available is worth questioning.",
      "action_taken": "Declined to counter Lightning Strike with No More Lies, taking 3 damage to face.",
      "better_line": "Counter Lightning Strike with No More Lies. The opponent can't pay {3} with only Rockface Village untapped, so it's a guaranteed exile. Preserving life total matters against a red deck that can burn you out, and No More Lies trading for Lightning Strike is a clean 1-for-1 at similar mana cost.",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 40,
      "player": "Gem3P Villain",
      "decision_index": 48,
