    {
      "severity": "moderate",
      "description": "Gem3P Villain declined to counter a Shock with No More Lies available. Shock deals 2 damage and at 17 life this matters, but more importantly, the opponent has very few cards and resources - countering their spells denies them tempo and card advantage. The opponent likely targeted Gem3P Villain directly (bringing them to 15) or could be targeting something relevant. With No More Lies costing only WU (which Gem3P has available via Hallowed Fountain + Island), there's little reason not to counter it. The 3 mana tax from No More Lies would almost certainly counter Shock since the opponent has 4 lands tapped (postcombat main). Additionally, letting damage through when you're already at 17 life against a red aggro deck is risky, especially when you have a 5-mana Elspeth you want to deploy next turn.",
